The MIT licence above covers the SOFTWARE in this repository only. Three other
things in and around this project are licensed differently, and the difference
matters more than the code does.

THE ARCHIVE'S OWN DATA — Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 (CC-BY-4.0)

  The work this project adds to the sheets: the georeferences and control
  points, the place names and labels read off them and reviewed by hand, the
  traced footprints, the gazetteer, and the catalogue metadata we wrote.

  Use it, including commercially, including modified. Credit the Vietnam Map
  Archive Project and link to https://maparchive.vn. Full text:
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  This is the part volunteers built, and attribution is what they are owed.

THE SCANNED SHEETS — not ours to license

  Each scan belongs to the institution that holds the paper and carries that
  institution's own terms. The holding institution and the source URL are
  recorded per sheet and shown on its catalogue page; check there, and with
  them, before reusing an image. A permissive licence on our code and our
  annotations says nothing about their scans.

THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE AND DATA

  Dependencies keep their own licences (see package.json and the lockfile).
  The basemap is built from OpenStreetMap data, © OpenStreetMap contributors,
  available under the Open Database License. The modern satellite imagery in
  the header and the map viewer is Esri's and is attributed in the interface.
